<!--
  D4 destructive deploy — component adds/updates (the coexistence-code going new-only).
  These deploy BETWEEN the Pre and Post destructive waves:
    sf project deploy start \
      --manifest manifest/d4-datetime-retire/package.xml \
      --pre-destructive-changes  manifest/d4-datetime-retire/destructiveChangesPre.xml \
      --post-destructive-changes manifest/d4-datetime-retire/destructiveChangesPost.xml \
      --test-level RunLocalTests
  Manifest mode (not --source-dir) is deliberate: it ignores source-tracking, so the
  local field-def/translation deletions and phantom conflicts do not interfere; org
  field deletion is driven solely by the destructive pair. Each listed component is a
  full-file replace whose new-only version removes the last old-field reference, so the
  Post wave can drop the 7 data fields with nothing referencing them.
-->
